    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d754">

                <pb facs="0856" n="744" xml:id="pg744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.114 Narcotics/1227: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-01T14:00:00-04:00">August 1, 1935—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>230. Your despatch No. 3648.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d754-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Report by radio date when new system of narcotic drug import certificates
                        will become effective.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Inform all consular offices in China that when new system becomes
                        effective prospective importers who are subject to extraterritorial
                        jurisdiction should continue to transmit through the American Consul the
                        same documentation as heretofore in addition to sending either directly or
                        through the American Consul the Chinese Government’s import permit. Consular
                        officers should inform regular importers from the United States.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
